Here's a JavaScript function that accepts text and posts messages via the Slack API to a specified channel:

```javascript
function postToSlack(text, channel) {
  const token = 'your_slack_api_token'; // Replace with your actual Slack API token
  const url = `https://slack.com/api/chat.postMessage?channel=${channel}&text=${encodeURIComponent(text)}&token=${token}`;

  fetch(url, {
    method: 'GET',
    headers: {
      'Content-Type': 'application/x-www-form-urlencoded'
    }
  })
    .then(response => response.json())
    .then(data => console.log('Message posted successfully:', data))
    .catch(error => console.error('Error posting message:', error));
}

// Example usage
postToSlack('Hello, world!', '#general');
```

Make sure to replace `'your_slack_api_token'` with your actual Slack API token. This function uses the `fetch` API to send a GET request to the Slack API with the provided text and channel. The response is then parsed as JSON and logged to the console. If there's an error, it will be caught and logged as well.

